<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison figure still sets the Muschelkalk shell beside the 25.60 µm ocellus field. The 12-bin orientation cosine is 0.995, so the edge-angle mix is broad in both images, but the radial KS remains 0.94: the photograph is not a picture of the cellular pigment. The GIF still carries the pattern as chroma on the shell." ;
